## Implementation Approach
1. Initialize per-tenant state and buffers when `beginTenant` is called
2. Route incoming messages to appropriate tenant join windows
3. Join 'orders' and 'payments' streams within 20-second windows
4. Emit reconciled results to 'tenant_reconciliations' topic
5. Track offsets per-tenant and commit independently
6. Implement error handling to isolate tenant failures
7. Include canary test with 3 messages to validate multi-tenant flow

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design multi-tenant throughput controls with backpressure and strong delivery guarantees in KCNA.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant isolation
- Token bucket rate limiting
- Backpressure signaling to producers
- Idempotent dedupe for at-least-once
- Quota-based configurability and Canary testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for per-tenant token bucket limiter
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, burst) {
    this.rate = rate; // tokens per second
    this.burst = burst;
    this.tokens = burst;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  allow() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.burst, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.last = now;
    if (this.tokens >= 1) {
      this.tokens -= 1;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
```

